deposit; online lending solutions for consumers and small businesses; customer service center services; an automated telephone banking system; and remote deposit capture and payroll services. Sierra Bancorp was founded in 1977 and is headquartered in Porterville, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin J. McPhaill | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 447 people. Revenue per employee of $347K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $72K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10). Recent headlines include layoff or workforce-reduction announcements.","financial_summary":["Sierra Bancorp is a small-cap financial services business with a $537M market cap on $155M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $32M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.80\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 8.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Recent layoff news \u2014 often the market\u2019s first signal that growth is under pressure or costs are being rebased","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["27 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"The 2027 Chevrolet Silverado 1500 and GMC Sierra 1500 Get Worse Fuel Economy Numbers","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/2027-chevrolet-silverado-1500-gmc-215846000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794006462.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.34,"